      "title": "Classes and Objects: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Classes and Objects: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Class vs Object",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Class== = blueprint: state (**fields**) + behavior (**methods**)",
                "==Object== = one instance, created at runtime",
                "==Constructor== runs on creation to initialise state",
                "No constructor defined → compiler adds a **no-arg default**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Instance field",
                "`static` member"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Belongs to",
                  "one object",
                  "the class"
                ],
                [
                  "Copies",
                  "{blue:one per object}",
                  "{purple:one, shared}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example: Create and Call",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Car c = new Car(\"red\");",
                "c.drive();"
              ],
              "note": "one object, method called through the reference c"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Gotcha: Reference ≠ Object",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Car a = new Car(\"red\");",
                "Car b = a;",
                "b.color = \"blue\";",
                "// a.color is now \"blue\""
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`b = a` copies the ==reference==, not the object",
                "Both point to the **same** object"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "A variable holds a ==reference==. Change through either name and **both** see it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Encapsulation and Abstraction",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Encapsulation and Abstraction",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Encapsulation",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Encapsulation== = data plus the methods that act on it, in one class",
                "Fields are {red:private}; outside code uses public methods",
                "Getters/setters ==validate input== and let internals change without breaking callers"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "private double balance;",
                "public void deposit(double x) {",
                "    if (x <= 0)",
                "        throw new IllegalArgumentException();",
                "    balance += x;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "balance can never get a bad value"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Abstraction vs Encapsulation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Abstraction== = expose **what** an object does, hide **how**",
                "Built with `abstract class` and `interface`",
                "Model only the ==essential behavior=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Encapsulation",
                "Abstraction"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Goal",
                  "Protect state",
                  "Simplify the design"
                ],
                [
                  "Idea",
                  "Information hiding",
                  "Essential behavior only"
                ],
                [
                  "Tool",
                  "`private` fields",
                  "abstract classes, interfaces"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Public getter returning the internal mutable list ==leaks state=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Return a copy",
              "text": "Return `List.copyOf(items)` or `Collections.unmodifiableList(items)`, never the raw list."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Inheritance and the super Keyword",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Inheritance and the super Keyword",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Inheritance Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Inheritance== = subclass reuses and extends a superclass",
                "Models **is-a**: a Dog is an Animal",
                "Syntax: `class Dog extends Animal`",
                "Subclass gets the {green:non-private} fields and methods"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. super and Single Inheritance",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`super(...)` calls the parent constructor: ==first statement== in the child constructor",
                "`super.method()` calls the **parent version** of a method",
                "Java allows ==one superclass== only",
                "Multiple behavior: implement **several interfaces**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class Dog extends Animal {",
                "  Dog() { super(\"Rex\"); }",
                "  void speak() {",
                "    super.speak();",
                "  }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "parent constructor first, then parent method"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Abstract Class vs Interface",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Abstract class",
                "Interface"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "State",
                  "fields + constructors",
                  "no instance state"
                ],
                [
                  "Purpose",
                  "shared base for related classes",
                  "contract for **unrelated** classes"
                ],
                [
                  "Inherit",
                  "`extends` one",
                  "`implements` many"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Gotcha: final",
              "text": "`final class` cannot be extended; `final` method cannot be overridden."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Polymorphism: Overloading vs Overriding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Polymorphism: Overloading vs Overriding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. One Interface, Many Forms",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Polymorphism== = one call, behaviour depends on the **object**",
                "{blue:Overloading}: same name, different parameters, same class; ==compile time== (static binding)",
                "{green:Overriding}: subclass redefines inherited method, same signature; ==runtime== (dynamic dispatch)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example: Runtime Type Wins",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class Animal { void speak() { print(\"...\"); } }",
                "class Dog extends Animal {",
                "  @Override void speak() { print(\"Woof\"); }",
                "}",
                "Animal a = new Dog();",
                "a.speak();"
              ],
              "note": "runtime type decides, not the reference type"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "Woof"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Overloading vs Overriding",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Overloading",
                "Overriding"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Where",
                  "same class",
                  "subclass"
                ],
                [
                  "Signature",
                  "different parameters",
                  "same signature"
                ],
                [
                  "Bound",
                  "compile time",
                  "runtime"
                ],
                [
                  "Return type",
                  "alone cannot overload",
                  "same or ==covariant=="
                ],
                [
                  "Access",
                  "any",
                  "no ==narrower== than parent"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Gotchas",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`static` methods are ==hidden==, not overridden",
                "`private` and `final` methods cannot be overridden"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Add @Override",
              "text": "A typo in the name or parameters becomes a **compile error**, not a silent new method."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Composition vs Inheritance",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Composition vs Inheritance",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Has-a vs Is-a",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Composition== = **has-a**: a field holds another object",
                "Work is **delegated** to it (Car has an Engine)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Inheritance",
                "Composition"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Relation",
                  "is-a",
                  "has-a"
                ],
                [
                  "Coupling",
                  "{red:tight}, compile-time",
                  "{green:loose}"
                ],
                [
                  "Swap at runtime",
                  "no",
                  "yes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example: Car has an Engine",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Engine is passed in; `start()` ==delegates== to it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class Car {",
                "  private Engine engine;",
                "  Car(Engine e) { this.engine = e; }",
                "  void start() { engine.start(); }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q"
                  ],
                  [
                    "a",
                    "b"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q": {
                    "text": "True is-a, parent contract kept?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "a": {
                    "text": "Inherit",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  "b": {
                    "text": "Compose",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "a",
                    "label": "yes"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q",
                    "to": "b",
                    "label": "no"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inheriting only to reuse code: ==fragile base class==, a parent change breaks every child",
                "Deep hierarchies are hard to follow: keep them ==shallow=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Default to composition",
              "text": "Type the field as an ==interface== so the part can be swapped at runtime."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "OOP Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "OOP Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Classes and Pillars",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Idea",
                "Remember"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Class",
                  "==blueprint==; object = one instance"
                ],
                [
                  "`static`",
                  "shared by the class"
                ],
                [
                  "Instance",
                  "one copy per object"
                ],
                [
                  "Encapsulation",
                  "`private` fields + public methods"
                ],
                [
                  "Abstraction",
                  "expose ==what==, hide how"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inheritance and Polymorphism",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inheritance = ==is-a==, `extends`, `super()`",
                "Reference type decides what you can **call**",
                "Object type decides which **override** runs"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Overriding",
                "Overloading"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Signature",
                  "same in the child",
                  "same name, different parameters"
                ],
                [
                  "Resolved",
                  "{blue:runtime}",
                  "{green:compile time}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Animal a = new Dog();",
                "a.speak(); // Dog.speak() runs",
                "a.fetch(); // compile error"
              ],
              "note": "Animal has no fetch()"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Choosing",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`extends` for ==is-a==, composition for ==has-a==",
                "Default to **composition**",
                "Use `@Override` and `final` deliberately"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "The ==reference type== sets what you can call; the ==object type== sets which override runs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`Animal a = new Dog(); a.speak(); a.fetch();` Dog overrides speak and adds fetch. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`a.speak()` runs Dog's version: the object type picks the override",
                "`a.fetch()` fails to compile: the reference type Animal has no fetch"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "After `Car b = a; b.color = \"blue\";`, what does `a.color` hold?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`blue`: `b = a` copies the reference, not the object",
                "Both names point at one Car"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A getter does `return items;` for a private list. Why is that still a leak?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Callers get the real list, so `getItems().clear()` empties your state",
                "Return `List.copyOf(items)` or an unmodifiable view"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Can `int f(int x)` overload `void f(int x)` in one class?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No: the parameter lists match, only the return type differs",
                "Overloads need different parameters"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
